vLLM 0.32.0 + DFlash2 context-lookup drafting, ported from HyperQwen (https://github.com/syv-ai/HyperQwen,
Apache-2.0, commit ce9615c, patches cut against vLLM 0.31.0). Apply to the installed vllm package directory with
`patch -p1` (setup-port.sh does this). Contents, from HyperQwen's patch series:

  speed-knobs-envs, vllm-pr50021-gdn-spec-bounds, spec-decode-attn, hybrid-kv-groups-v2-cudagraph,
  dflash2-lookup-drafting, hybrid-sw-block-promote, offload-dflash-eagle-groups, dflash2-ngram-chains,
  dflash2-prewarm, mamba-chunked-prefill-align (one hunk dropped: already in 0.32), dflash2-z-adaptive-emitted,
  vllm-pr61050-lru-running-prefix

Changes for 0.32: the model_runner draft-count hunk rebased onto 0.32's draft-token slicing; the spec-decode-attn
FA hunk moved to FlashAttentionImpl.forward (fuzzy apply had put it in do_kv_cache_update); DFlash2Speculator.propose()
takes 0.32's dp_sync_state and num_speculative_tokens.

Also (not from HyperQwen): the qwen3 reasoning parser honours a think block the chat template already closed in
the prompt (e.g. DavidAU's {REASON:i...} instruct modes); before, such output was all filed as reasoning.
parser/qwen3.py, parser/abstract_parser.py (DelegatingParser forwards set_prompt_token_ids), parser/engine/adapters.py.

